 populace often don't  offer real solutions  you know Trump talks about undocumented  Mexican migrants in the United States  but in fact their net migration in  recent years has been zero and they take  jobs that Americans don't want and the  American economy is built on under  relatively cheap labor or if you took  you know in some of Europeans who are  promoting Islamophobia as an answer to  terrorism you just have hair builders  talking in those terms but of course the  last thing you want to do if you want to  fight terrorism effectively is to  discriminate against the Muslim  community because they're the ones the  most like beaten though  the stage of a potential tour spot the  police need their cooperation which they  won't get if official government policy  is Lama is Islamophobic so what we need  is for the public for both practical  reasons but also reasons of principle to  stand up to these populist is to say  these are not the answers to our  problems and these are not the kind of  intolerant hatred filled societies that  we want to live in we want to thank you  very much for your perspective Kenneth  Roth the executive director of Human  Rights Watch you have said that human  rights is under threat in leading  democracies due to the rise of populism  and we very much appreciate your  perspective
 

